The rule for conformance.kernel.recovery states: "The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text" [65ae18af7a738b26]. However, the fence content must parse as JSON to be scored directly. In the input from cell fence[ A S ] B, the fence contains object A followed by sentence S, making it unparseable as strict JSON. The recovery falls back to finding top-level objects in the text, where B (outside the fence) is the last top-level object and gets recovered. In the rewritten text, B is removed, leaving only the unparseable fence. Recovery then falls back to extracting A as the last top-level object from within the fence content. Therefore, the recovered object moves from B to A.